# unfer_edge environment. Copy to /etc/unfer/edge.env, chmod 600, own by root.
#
# Every key here is OPTIONAL. unfer_edge starts with none of them set, using the
# built-in defaults, and `GET /version` reports which layer won for each key. An
# unset key is a supported configuration, not an omission.
#
# ── Networking ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Omit to accept the default. Set to 127.0.0.1 to refuse external connections.
# UNFER_LISTEN=0.0.0.0:3000

# Upstream this gateway proxies to. Omit only when unfer_edge is the only service
# on the host; with no upstream, every non-self-service route 502s.
# UNFER_BACKEND=127.0.0.1:3001

# ── S22 admin console (requires the `audit` feature) ─────────────────────────
# The principal the admin console is minted for. Defaults to `operator`.
# Omit ONLY if you have deliberately decided the console runs unprivileged --
# it is minted exactly once at startup and cannot be re-minted later.
# UNFER_ADMIN_PRINCIPAL=operator

# ── Capabilities ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where a preset roster is discovered. Omit to run with inline grants only.
# UNFER_PRESETS_DIR=/etc/unfer/presets

# ── Credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT here. Secrets belong in the vault (S27) and reach the process through
# UNFER_SECRET_* at runtime; see DEPLOY.md "Secrets". A secret committed to this
# file, or baked into a unit with `Environment=`, is in the process table, in
# `systemctl show`, and in every core dump -- none of which are access-controlled
# the way the vault is.

# ── Diagnostics ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anything not consumed as a config key is ignored by the config loader, so
# RUST_LOG can live here safely.
# RUST_LOG=info
